course: dictionary
lesson: 10092
title: Theropods: the two-legged dinosaurs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A theropod is a member of a large group of dinosaurs that walked on two legs. Tyrannosaurus rex and Velociraptor are both theropods, so they belong to the same family.
explain: The sentence «Birds evolved from small feathered meat-eating dinosaurs called theropods» gives you clues. Feathered, meat-eating and dinosaurs tell you what kind of animal a theropod was: a dinosaur with feathers that mostly ate other animals.
explain: Read the sentence again to check. It says theropods are «the group of T. rex and Velociraptor». When a sentence names examples, use them to test your meaning. Theropod is a noun (a theropod, theropods), and it can also describe things, as in «theropod footprints».
fact: A theropod is a member of a large group of dinosaurs that walked on two legs.
fact: Most theropods were meat-eaters, such as Tyrannosaurus rex, Velociraptor and Allosaurus.
fact: Birds are living theropods: scientists say birds evolved from small feathered theropod dinosaurs.
fact: Theropods had hollow bones, three main toes, and sharp teeth or beaks; many had feathers.
fact: «Theropod» can be a noun («a large theropod») or an adjective («theropod footprints»).
exercise: What is a theropod? | A type of fish that lives in deep water | A plant that grows in the desert | *A member of a large group of dinosaurs that walked on two legs | A tool scientists use to dig up bones
exercise: «Birds evolved from small feathered meat-eating dinosaurs called theropods.» What do scientists say about birds? | They have no feathers and no bones | They are not related to dinosaurs | They cannot fly at all | *They are living theropods
exercise: Which animal is a theropod? | A giant tortoise | *Velociraptor | Woolly mammoth | A wolf
test: Which of these is a feature of theropods? | Shells on their backs | Gills for breathing under water | Wings made only of skin | *Hollow bones and three main toes
test: «Theropod footprints» were found in the mud. What does theropod describe here? | *Footprints left by theropod dinosaurs | Footprints left by a woolly mammoth | Footprints left by fish | Footprints made by a giant tortoise
exam: In which sentence is theropod used to describe something? | A robin is a living theropod | *The museum has theropod footprints in the mud | Velociraptor was a theropod | Theropods had sharp teeth
